---
import Eyebrow from "./Eyebrow.astro";
import Card from "./Card.astro";
---

<section
  class="mx-auto flex w-full max-w-page flex-col gap-stack px-gutter pt-section"
>
  <Eyebrow>Local by construction</Eyebrow>

  <h2 class="max-w-[760px] font-display text-h2">
    None of it leaves machines you own.
  </h2>

  <div class="mt-[22px] grid grid-cols-1 gap-cards lg:grid-cols-3">
    <Card title="No account">
      Nothing to sign up for and nothing to sign in to. When machines do need
      to know who is asking, the answer is your own Tailscale login &mdash; not
      a credential GitWarren issued and not one it stores.
    </Card>
    <Card title="Nothing cached">
      Every branch name, commit and diff on screen is read from git at the moment
      it is shown &mdash; so nothing can quietly go stale behind your back.
    </Card>
    <Card title="One SQLite file per machine">
      A machine&#39;s reviews and comments live in a single file in its
      application-data directory, beside the code they are about. Delete it and
      GitWarren is gone from that machine. Your repositories are untouched.
    </Card>
  </div>
</section>
